{
  "id": 88054281,
  "iid": 2051,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Moving glib.h out of extern C",
  "description": "With the new version of glib2(glib2-2.67.3), having #include <glib.h> inside extern \"C\" {} creates a build error: template with C linkage. Moving glib.h outside the extern \"C\" fixes this issue and AFAICT does not break anything else with older glib2. I tested this on Fedora builds in Rawhide on wireshark-3.4.3. (Sorry about the mess with the previous merge request)",
  "state": "merged",
